# Snyk Code (SAST) exclusion.
#
# The `ignore:` entries above apply to dependency findings only - they are inert
# for Snyk Code (verified empirically), so a rule-level ignore cannot be used here.
# Snyk Code also reads only the scan-root policy file, so this block cannot live in
# external/ag-shared/.snyk even though that directory is a subrepo shared with
# ag-grid, ag-charts and ag-studio: the same block must be maintained in all three
# repository roots.
#
# scripts/snyk-viewer/index.mjs is a manually-run, localhost-only (binds 127.0.0.1)
# developer tool for viewing Snyk reports. It is never built, shipped or deployed.
# Snyk Code reports 9 javascript/PT path-traversal findings in it whose stated cause
# - "unsanitized input from the HTTP request body flows into fs.readFileSync" - is
# false: every flagged sink is guarded by a resolve() + containment check + filename
# check before the read or write. A correct realpath-based rewrite was implemented
# and scanned, and it did not clear the findings, so no reasonable code change will.
#
# This excludes the whole file from Snyk Code, not just javascript/PT, so a genuine
# future finding in it would also be hidden. Accepted because the tool is local-only
# dev tooling. Revisit if it ever becomes something that runs outside a developer
# machine.
exclude:
  code:
    - external/ag-shared/scripts/snyk-viewer/index.mjs
